The decisive correction is that the second component is not an α-chlorocyclopentenone. SELFIES decoding gives a chloroperoxybenzoic acid (mCPBA-type oxidant), while dichloromethane is solvent and water is work-up. The large substrate contains a pyridine nitrogen and a tertiary amide/lactam nitrogen; mCPBA most plausibly oxidizes the pyridine N to its N-oxide. I will record this validated interpretation and then review the stored evidence before giving the product.

